WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.630
Jack-Jack crashing Edna's fashion show, the
return of Kari the babysitter, and the reveal

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:10.150
of Frozone's wife are just some of the amazing
scenes cut from Pixar's Incredibles 2.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.570
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video I'll be revealing and explaining

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.460
five Incredibles 2 deleted scenes that you
probably wish Pixar had included in the movie.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.489
Plus keep watching to the end for an extra
Edna and Jack-Jack clip where I'll reveal

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.699
two new Jack-Jack powers we never saw in the
main movie.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:30.970
If this is your first time here, I do regular
deep dives into your favourite Pixar, Disney

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.850
and superhero movies so tap the bell to keep
up to date with all my new videos.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:36.850
"FROZONE: Honey?"

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:37.850
"What?"

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:38.850
"FROZONE: Where's my supersuit?"

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.850
"I had to..

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:40.850
I'm washing it!"

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.850
"FROZONE: Don't lie to me!

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:48.429
I keep that suit spotless!"

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:57.156
"FROZONE: And you better not be trying to
hide it on me!"

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:58.156
"It.. it was filthy!"

00:00:58.156 --> 00:00:59.156
"FROZONE: It was next to godliness clean and
ready for action!"

00:00:59.156 --> 00:01:00.156
"I'm not playing with you."

00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:01.156
"It was filthy!"

00:01:01.156 --> 00:01:02.156
"How dare you?!"

00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:03.156
"How dare you.."

00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:04.156
"Aha!"

00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:05.156
"Lucius don't you think you can get away from
me!"

00:01:05.156 --> 00:01:06.156
"Lucius!"

00:01:06.156 --> 00:01:13.690
Now, I 
really wish this scene had been in the movie.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.900
It's a wonderful callback to that hilarious
scene in the first Incredibles where Frozone

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.910
goes searching for his supersuit after looking
out the window and seeing Syndrome's Omnidroid

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.500
wreaking havoc on the city.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.890
"Where is my supersuit?"

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.900
"HONEY: I put it away."

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.140
This time around it's Honey who spots the
Underminer's enormous drilling machine causing

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.390
chaos and who then hilariously and frantically
tries to find somewhere to hide Frozone's

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.390
suit.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.450
I think it would have been nice to see the
woman behind the voice especially as she was

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.280
such huge hit with fans in the first movie.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.530
Incredibles 2 director Brad Bird has said
this original scene took too much momentum

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.360
away from the Underminer action sequence at
the beginning of the movie and he felt that,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.460
in the end, Honey was funnier as a voice as
that way everyone who watches the film can

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.040
have their own idea of what she looks like.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.920
Although I can see Bird's perspective up to
a point and I enjoyed Incredibles 2, I can't

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.729
help but think this extra scene with Honey
would have just been fantastic.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:14.500
Fun fact: The design for Honey in this deleted
clip was actually reused later in the movie

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.490
for one of the other supers who assemble on
the Deavor's yacht.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.690
Edna and Jack-Jack's scenes together are some
of the funniest in Incredibles 2 and there's

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:27.060
some amazing bonus material on the Blu-ray
which reveals some great extra scenes with

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.500
the two characters.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.890
The first is a deleted scene where Edna is
hosting her own fashion show which Jack-Jack

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.390
accidentally and amusingly interrupts.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.930
"E, I'm operating on no sleep."

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.590
"I'm telling you this baby is freaking me
out!"

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.590
"Yes."

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.050
"I don't know where he's gonna be, I don't
know what he's gonna be."

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.050
"Robert!"

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.080
"Anything can happen and I've got to respond."

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.080
"Robert!"

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.080
"What, what?"

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.080
"The baby is gone."

00:02:53.080 --> 00:03:03.080
"What is it Humphrey?"

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:21.130
"They're going crazy, they want you to take
a bow."

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.880
"And they want the glitter baby."

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.470
"No glitter baby!"

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.930
"First the team will bow, then the junior
designers, then I will come."

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.790
"No glitter baby."

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.270
This is a great scene that I'm sure many fans
would have loved to have seen in the final

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.270
film.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.709
It shows how Edna's real passion is designing
outfits for Supers, but because they're illegal

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:45.710
she has to work with supermodels who we already
know that Edna has very little regard for:

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:46.730
"Supermodels."

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.340
"Nothing super about them."

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:54.620
"Spoiled, stupid little stick-figures with
poofy lips who think only about themselves."

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.390
Plus, seeing Jack-Jack turn into a "Glitter
Baby" would have been really fun and I wonder

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.650
if it's supposed to be an additional power
we didn't see in the movie.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.370
We did see Jack-Jack's mimicry powers when
he transforms his appearance into a reflection

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:11.130
of Edna, but this feels like it might be a
kind of adaptive or camouflaging-type power.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:15.880
Incredibles 2 is Pixar's longest film to date
and I suspect this scene was cut because the

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.079
movie was pretty packed.

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:21.239
Although we do get some fantastic moments
with Edna and Jack-Jack in the final film,

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.000
it's always great to see more!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.830
By the way, the clothes in Edna's fashion
line "Mode" were worn by models but still

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.530
drew inspiration from the powers of Edna's
favourite clients: Superheroes.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:34.259
For example, the see-through chiffon around
this model's head was inspired by the look

00:04:34.259 --> 00:04:36.380
of a force field.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.819
Next up is a deleted scene that's perhaps
a bit dark where we discover what happened

00:04:39.819 --> 00:04:42.349
to Kari the Babysitter after the first movie.

00:04:42.349 --> 00:04:43.430
"Hi Nancy!"

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.060
"Oh, Helen, Bob!"

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.080
"I hope we're not interrupting dinner."

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.900
"Actually, we'd like to talk to Kari about.."

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.610
"We thought it might be best if we just dropped
by."

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.090
"You were supposed to be back late in the
evening.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:57.020
You left her in charge of your baby overnight
and into the next day."

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.169
"Well I'm sorry about that.

00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:00.389
That was not planned."

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:01.509
"The er..

00:05:01.509 --> 00:05:03.300
The kids kind of surprised me."

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.199
"That took us by surprise as well.

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:11.669
A baby's a lot of responsibility for a teenager
and I think Kari got a bit overwhelmed."

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:12.669
"She was hysterical."

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:13.770
"She calmed down."

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.120
"She's been twitchy ever since."

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.660
"Hello Mr and Mrs Parr."

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.110
"Kari, just the girl I wanted to see.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:23.120
We were talking about when you were babysitting
for us.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.849
Did you notice anything odd about Jack-Jack?"

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:29.309
"Not that I remember.

00:05:29.309 --> 00:05:30.309
It's a blank."

00:05:30.309 --> 00:05:33.870
"But all those phone messages you left us."

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.169
"Phone messages?"

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:37.060
"You don't remember?"

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.750
"No, oh op."

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.680
"Was that no?"

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.680
"What?"

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.680
"Jack-Jack?"

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:45.680
"Ha, ha!"

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.599
"That's what I'm talking about, twitchy!"

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:52.629
Kari's role in the first Incredibles movie
was expanded when she featured in the short

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:57.439
film Jack-Jack Attack which showed her discovering
baby Parr's superpowers and then having her

00:05:57.439 --> 00:05:59.490
memory wiped by Rick Dicker.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.360
This deleted scene from Incredibles 2 is pretty
dark because it looks like Dicker's memory

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.659
erasing might have really messed Kari up.

00:06:06.659 --> 00:06:10.660
Kari's obviously a fan favourite character
especially since appearing in the Jack-Jack

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:15.099
short so I think many Pixar fans would have
liked a chance to catch up and find out what

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:16.099
happened to her.

00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:20.099
However, the answer is a little unsettling
to say the least and given this scene was

00:06:20.099 --> 00:06:24.939
one of the filmmakers' options for opening
the movie, I can see why Pixar ended up scrapping

00:06:24.939 --> 00:06:25.939
it.

00:06:25.939 --> 00:06:29.559
There's an interesting action scene cut out
of the final movie where Edna's high-tech

00:06:29.559 --> 00:06:36.990
systems [at her home] begin attacking her
and Mr Incredible.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:07:10.240
"I've lost control of my security system!"

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.879
The theme that Bird wanted to explore in this
deleted scene was the idea of artificial intelligence

00:07:14.879 --> 00:07:17.110
systems turning against their human creators.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.509
If you feel this sounds familiar, you're right
because it's pretty much what happened when

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:25.470
Syndrome's Omnidroid turned against him in
The Incredibles.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.830
Initially, this artificial intelligence theme
was actually the main story for the sequel.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:33.580
In this cut scene, Bird wanted to show what
could happen if high tech systems like the

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.139
ones Edna has became corrupted.

00:07:36.139 --> 00:07:37.690
This idea of corrupted A.I.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.610
was eventually abandoned though in favour
of the Screenslaver villain plot, perhaps

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.979
because it might have felt too similar to
the Omnidroid twist from the first movie.

00:07:45.979 --> 00:07:50.349
This action scene, which has vibes of James
Bond about it, does look pretty cool though,

00:07:50.349 --> 00:07:52.419
and Bird has said he might still explore the
A.I.

00:07:52.419 --> 00:07:54.870
idea in another movie.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:59.589
Incredibles 2 opens at a very fast pace, pretty
much picking up with the Parr's facing off

00:07:59.589 --> 00:08:01.310
against the Underminer.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:05.689
However, originally, Bird planned to kick
the movie off at the Parr family home and

00:08:05.689 --> 00:08:08.389
remind us of how it was destroyed during the
battle with Syndrome.

00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:14.900
"I hate to cut short a tender moment, but
unless you wanna explain this to a crowd?"

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.369
"Come on!"

00:08:17.369 --> 00:08:24.249
"When they notice I'm gone, just say I went
to call Dicker, OK?"

00:08:24.249 --> 00:08:25.860
"Hmm, OK."

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.469
"Hmm, Dicker."

00:08:27.469 --> 00:08:33.110
"Mr Dicker, it's me, Violet, Violet Parr.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:43.539
You know how you just drove us to our house
and my parents are superheroes?"

00:08:43.539 --> 00:08:44.720
"Sure kid."

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:45.910
"Yes, yes!

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.690
The extraction point.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.690
Down!

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.250
They'll know where that is."

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:55.070
Although it's a fun clip, it's not as good
as the action-packed opening scene we did

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:59.009
get, especially as it doesn't tie in so well
with the very end of the first movie where

00:08:59.009 --> 00:09:01.630
the Underminer suddenly popped up.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:06.070
And here's the bonus Edna and Jack-Jack scene
from the Auntie Edna short which shows what

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:10.300
happened the night after Bob left Jack-Jack
with Edna while he got some sleep.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.070
"OK, come out and show me."

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.069
"Walk it, yes.

00:09:15.069 --> 00:09:16.550
There it is.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.040
The room is yours."

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.660
"They are lucky to be in your presence."

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.050
"Now the turn.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.050
Yes!

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:27.350
You are a tiny god!"

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:33.410
"Dada is here.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:38.180
Let's show him how fabulous you look."

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:43.839
That turn Edna gets Jack-Jack to do is just
adorable and when she calls him a "tiny god",

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.690
it's a call-back to the first movie where
Edna was frustrated with not being able to

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.970
legally design for supers anymore.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:50.970
"Feh!

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.399
I used to design for gods."

00:09:53.399 --> 00:09:58.120
Also, notice in this scene how Edna has been
making a list of all of Jack-Jack's powers.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:03.150
The movie revealed at the end that Jack-Jack
has a total of 17 powers and, so far Edna

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:07.770
seems to have 14 of them on her list, but
intriguingly there's two new ones listed under

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.801
Edna's "Elemental Shift" category called "Smoke"
and "Liquid".

00:10:10.801 --> 00:10:14.750
A promo spot for the Blu-ray release shows
what these look like.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:19.480
It appears that Jack-Jack can turn into smoke
allowing a ball that Edna tosses at him to

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.980
pass right through him.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:24.570
Then there's a shot of Jack-Jack where it
looks like he can even turn into a literal

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:25.889
water baby.

00:10:25.889 --> 00:10:29.889
These two powers didn't show up in Incredibles
2, but if you'd like a full breakdown of all

00:10:29.889 --> 00:10:35.100
of Jack-Jack's other 17 powers, tap here to
watch my Jack-Jack Powers Explained video

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.570
or click the link in the video description
below.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:41.490
Now, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had been included in the movie?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.190
Let me know what you think of them in the
comments below!

